{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"The claim is historically true: many white people have resisted oppressive governments. Examples include the White Rose movement against Nazi Germany, dissidents such as Václav Havel opposing communist rule in Czechoslovakia, and white South Africans who fought apartheid.\n\nIt’s a broad claim, though. It establishes that some white people resisted oppression—not that all did, that resistance was uniquely white, or that race caused their resistance. Others supported those same governments. The clearest assessment focuses on particular people, movements, and actions."}}
